            "review_title": "Review at The Artisan Buon Dua Le Cafe",
            "review_text": "Jonesy1974\nMold, United Kingdom510 contributions\n0\nVery good, great spot\nFeb 2019 • Couples\nHad a meal in here tonight. It was very enjoyable. Great spot on the balcony, looking down on the street below, people watching. We had some spring rolls to start with, which were absolutely delicious. We then had stewed pork in a clay pot and bun cha, both good. One reason we choose this place was the cheaper wine you can get. A glass of local plonk is 65000, which is pretty good for Hanoi. \nWe did ask for the dessert menu but it never arrived. But I don’t blame them as they just had some big parties in and it suddenly went very busy and they were rushed off their feet. Overall very good and would recommend.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 27, 2019",
